const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 6 Walkthrough: Candy Shop";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 6 walkthrough for the Candy Shop: the eight candy dispensers, the jar you fill in the right colour order, the four-wheel lock that takes 6841, and the letter board that gives the exit code G6H8.";
const faqJsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the exit code in Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 6 Candy Shop?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "G6H8. The candy shop's exit is not a number pad: the panel beside the pink arched door shows four character slots, and the four characters you need are the four labelled discs on the wooden 5x5 board — G, 6, H and 8. Type them in that order and the exit icon lights up on the door."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the four-digit code on the yellow drawer lock?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "6841. The lock is the row of four digit wheels inside the yellow display drawer, and the number comes from weighing the jar of candy you fill at the dispenser wall. Our recording shows the wheels reading 6, 8, 4 and 1 on two separate frames before the drawer is opened."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I fill the candy jar?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Take the empty jar from the present that lifts off the counter, stand it under the eight-canister dispenser wall and pull the levers in the order the game's paper clue shows. Each lever drops a layer of one colour into the jar and the layers stack bottom to top. In our recording the jar could not be emptied once a colour went in, so read the clue before you start pulling levers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How many candy dispensers are there?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Eight, in one row under a single yellow canopy. Each canister holds one colour and has its own black-topped lever underneath. They are the only place in the shop where you can add colour to the jar, and the order you pull them is the whole puzzle."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the memory game in the Candy Shop?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A card-matching mini-game on a red board: a grid of ice-cream and cupcake tiles that you flip over in pairs. The recording plays it twice — the second play is what releases the item you need — and the grid resets face down between attempts. Nothing in the room tells you which card is which, so it is pure memory."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Why can't I open the pink door?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Because the door is the last thing in the level, not the first. It opens only after the four-slot panel beside it has been filled with G6H8, and that code only exists once the labelled discs on the wooden 5x5 board have been placed. Tapping the door before then does nothing at all, and there is no message telling you why."}}]};
